1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,520
Welcome to Unit Five of Algebra One:
linear functions.

2
00:00:03,970 --> 00:00:07,917
In this lesson, we'll learn about slope,
which measures how steep a line is.

3
00:00:09,067 --> 00:00:13,886
A rate of change compares how much one
quantity changes to how much another

4
00:00:13,886 --> 00:00:14,400
changes.

5
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:19,321
If you save twenty dollars every week,
your savings grow at twenty dollars per

6
00:00:19,321 --> 00:00:19,607
week.

7
00:00:20,733 --> 00:00:26,553
For a line, the rate of change is called
the slope. Slope equals rise over run: the

8
00:00:26,553 --> 00:00:29,288
change in y divided by the change in x.

9
00:00:29,738 --> 00:00:35,263
As a formula, m equals y two minus y one,
over x two minus x one.

10
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:39,643
Find the slope through one comma two and
four comma eight.

11
00:00:40,093 --> 00:00:45,831
The change in y is eight minus two, which
is six. The change in x is four minus one,

12
00:00:45,831 --> 00:00:46,855
which is three.

13
00:00:47,305 --> 00:00:49,887
Six over three is two. So the slope is
two.

14
00:00:51,033 --> 00:00:54,895
Now through negative two comma five and
two comma negative three.

15
00:00:55,345 --> 00:01:00,631
The change in y is negative three minus
five, negative eight. The change in x is

16
00:01:00,631 --> 00:01:05,521
four. The slope is negative two, so the
line goes down from left to right.

17
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:10,549
A horizontal line has slope zero, because
y doesn't change.

18
00:01:10,999 --> 00:01:16,142
A vertical line has an undefined slope,
because the run is zero, and we can't

19
00:01:16,142 --> 00:01:17,143
divide by zero.

20
00:01:18,267 --> 00:01:23,020
Your turn. Find the slope of the line
through negative one comma four and three

21
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:23,621
comma six.

22
00:01:24,071 --> 00:01:25,522
Pause the video and try it.

23
00:01:25,972 --> 00:01:31,162
The change in y is two, and the change in
x is four. The slope is two over four,

24
00:01:31,162 --> 00:01:32,329
which is one half.

25
00:01:33,466 --> 00:01:37,541
Let's find a rate of change from a table
and decide whether it's constant.

26
00:01:38,966 --> 00:01:44,022
A car's fuel is recorded. At zero miles it
has fourteen gallons, at sixty miles

27
00:01:44,022 --> 00:01:49,334
twelve, at one hundred fifty miles nine,
and at two hundred forty miles six. Is the

28
00:01:49,334 --> 00:01:53,110
rate of change constant? What is it, and
what does it mean?

29
00:01:54,233 --> 00:02:00,030
Rate of change is the change in y over the
change in x. For the first pair, negative

30
00:02:00,030 --> 00:02:03,342
two over sixty, which is negative one
thirtieth.

31
00:02:04,466 --> 00:02:09,117
The second pair: negative three over
ninety, also negative one thirtieth.

32
00:02:10,266 --> 00:02:13,039
The third pair: negative three over ninety
again.

33
00:02:14,166 --> 00:02:18,874
The rate is the same every time, so the
relationship is linear, with slope

34
00:02:18,874 --> 00:02:21,355
negative one thirtieth gallon per mile.

35
00:02:22,499 --> 00:02:27,636
The rate is constant: negative one
thirtieth of a gallon per mile. In words,

36
00:02:27,636 --> 00:02:30,542
the car uses one gallon every thirty
miles.

37
00:02:31,666 --> 00:02:36,787
Watch out. Subtract in the same order on
top and bottom. The x values here are not

38
00:02:36,787 --> 00:02:41,971
evenly spaced, so you have to compute each
ratio rather than eyeball the table. And

39
00:02:41,971 --> 00:02:44,594
always interpret the slope with its units.

40
00:02:45,733 --> 00:02:51,205
Your turn. x values two, five, eleven have
y values seven, sixteen, thirty four. Is

41
00:02:51,205 --> 00:02:55,951
the rate of change constant, and what is
it? Pause the video and try it.

42
00:03:00,499 --> 00:03:05,298
Nine over three is three, and eighteen
over six is three. It's constant, with

43
00:03:05,298 --> 00:03:06,046
slope three.

44
00:03:07,166 --> 00:03:11,020
In this lesson, we'll learn the most
popular way to write a line:

45
00:03:11,020 --> 00:03:12,265
slope-intercept form.

46
00:03:13,399 --> 00:03:19,992
y equals m x plus b. m is the slope, and b
is the y intercept, where the line crosses

47
00:03:19,992 --> 00:03:20,845
the y axis.

48
00:03:21,966 --> 00:03:27,363
To graph y equals two x plus one, start at
the y intercept, zero comma one.

49
00:03:27,813 --> 00:03:33,034
The slope two means rise two, run one.
Plot another point at one comma three, and

50
00:03:33,034 --> 00:03:33,936
draw the line.

51
00:03:35,066 --> 00:03:40,783
Now graph y equals negative two thirds x
plus four. Start at zero comma four.

52
00:03:41,233 --> 00:03:45,760
The slope says go down two and right
three, to three comma two. Connect the

53
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:46,183
points.

54
00:03:47,299 --> 00:03:51,587
To write the equation from a graph, read
the y intercept and count the slope.

55
00:03:52,037 --> 00:03:57,656
This line crosses at negative three, and
rises one for every two across. So y

56
00:03:57,656 --> 00:03:59,845
equals one half x minus three.

57
00:04:00,966 --> 00:04:03,846
If an equation isn't in this form, solve
for y.

58
00:04:04,296 --> 00:04:09,908
Three x plus y equals five becomes y
equals negative three x plus five. The

59
00:04:09,908 --> 00:04:13,875
slope is negative three, and the y
intercept is five.

60
00:04:14,999 --> 00:04:19,885
Your turn. Find the slope and y intercept
of two x plus y equals seven.

61
00:04:20,335 --> 00:04:21,785
Pause the video and try it.

62
00:04:22,235 --> 00:04:28,333
Subtract two x: y equals negative two x
plus seven. The slope is negative two, and

63
00:04:28,333 --> 00:04:30,193
the y intercept is seven.

64
00:04:31,333 --> 00:04:35,822
Here's a worked example: rewrite an
equation in slope intercept form, then

65
00:04:35,822 --> 00:04:36,368
graph it.

66
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:43,048
Write four x minus three y equals nine in
slope intercept form, and graph it.

67
00:04:44,166 --> 00:04:47,558
Get y alone. First subtract four x from
both sides.

68
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:50,876
Divide every term by negative three.

69
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:57,403
Negative over negative is positive, so the
slope is four thirds, and the intercept is

70
00:04:57,403 --> 00:04:58,357
negative three.

71
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:04,829
To graph, start at the y intercept, zero,
negative three. Then rise four and run

72
00:05:04,829 --> 00:05:06,561
three to reach three, one.

73
00:05:07,700 --> 00:05:12,926
The equation is y equals four thirds x
minus three. Draw the line through zero,

74
00:05:12,926 --> 00:05:14,910
negative three and three, one.

75
00:05:16,033 --> 00:05:20,914
Watch out. When you divide by the
coefficient of y, divide every term. Watch

76
00:05:20,914 --> 00:05:26,180
the signs: negative divided by negative is
positive. And check one of your graphed

77
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:28,236
points in the original equation.

78
00:05:29,366 --> 00:05:34,947
Your turn. Write five x plus two y equals
negative six in slope intercept form.

79
00:05:34,947 --> 00:05:36,854
Pause the video and try it.

80
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:47,352
Subtract five x and divide by two: y
equals negative five halves x minus three.

81
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:52,879
When you know one point on a line and its
slope, point-slope form writes the

82
00:05:52,879 --> 00:05:54,089
equation in one step.

83
00:05:55,233 --> 00:05:59,905
The form is y minus y one equals m times x
minus x one.

84
00:06:00,355 --> 00:06:04,579
Here, x one comma y one is a point on the
line, and m is the slope.

85
00:06:05,700 --> 00:06:08,452
Write the line through two comma five with
slope three.

86
00:06:08,902 --> 00:06:14,001
Plug in: y minus five equals three times x
minus two. That's the equation.

87
00:06:15,133 --> 00:06:19,187
To convert to slope-intercept form,
distribute and solve for y.

88
00:06:19,637 --> 00:06:26,015
y minus five equals three x minus six. Add
five: y equals three x minus one.

89
00:06:27,133 --> 00:06:32,292
Given two points, find the slope first.
Through one comma negative one and three

90
00:06:32,292 --> 00:06:35,773
comma three, the slope is four over two,
which is two.

91
00:06:36,223 --> 00:06:43,007
Then y plus one equals two times x minus
one. Simplify: y equals two x minus three.

92
00:06:44,133 --> 00:06:49,096
Careful with negative coordinates. Through
negative four comma two with slope one

93
00:06:49,096 --> 00:06:49,403
half:

94
00:06:49,853 --> 00:06:55,954
y minus two equals one half times x plus
four. Subtracting a negative becomes plus.

95
00:06:57,100 --> 00:07:02,000
Your turn. Write the equation of the line
through two comma one and four comma

96
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,948
seven, in slope-intercept form.

97
00:07:04,398 --> 00:07:05,849
Pause the video and try it.

98
00:07:06,299 --> 00:07:12,517
The slope is six over two, which is three.
y minus one equals three times x minus

99
00:07:12,517 --> 00:07:15,280
two, so y equals three x minus five.

100
00:07:16,400 --> 00:07:20,859
Let's write the equation of a line through
two points, using point slope form.

101
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:27,190
Write an equation of the line through
negative two, seven and four, negative

102
00:07:27,190 --> 00:07:30,407
two, in point slope form and slope
intercept form.

103
00:07:31,533 --> 00:07:36,821
First the slope: negative two minus seven,
over four minus negative two. That's

104
00:07:36,821 --> 00:07:38,360
negative nine over six.

105
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,463
Simplify to negative three halves.

106
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:47,997
Use point slope form with the point
negative two, seven. y minus seven equals

107
00:07:47,997 --> 00:07:52,904
negative three halves times x minus
negative two, which is x plus two.

108
00:07:54,033 --> 00:07:57,020
Distribute: negative three halves x minus
three.

109
00:07:58,167 --> 00:08:02,903
Add seven to both sides. y equals negative
three halves x plus four.

110
00:08:04,033 --> 00:08:10,203
In point slope form, y minus seven equals
negative three halves times x plus two. In

111
00:08:10,203 --> 00:08:14,977
slope intercept form, y equals negative
three halves x plus four.

112
00:08:16,100 --> 00:08:21,327
Watch out. x minus negative two becomes x
plus two. Either point works in point

113
00:08:21,327 --> 00:08:25,231
slope form. And the best check is the
point you didn't use.

114
00:08:26,367 --> 00:08:31,149
Your turn. Write the line through one,
negative four and three, six in slope

115
00:08:31,149 --> 00:08:33,855
intercept form. Pause the video and try
it.

116
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:45,112
The slope is ten over two, which is five.
y plus four equals five times x minus one,

117
00:08:45,112 --> 00:08:47,509
so y equals five x minus nine.

118
00:08:48,633 --> 00:08:53,719
Lines can also be written in standard
form. In this lesson, we'll use it to find

119
00:08:53,719 --> 00:08:54,926
intercepts quickly.

120
00:08:56,066 --> 00:09:01,442
Standard form is A x plus B y equals C,
where A, B and C are integers.

121
00:09:01,892 --> 00:09:04,964
For example, two x plus three y equals
twelve.

122
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:11,156
The x intercept is where the line crosses
the x axis, so y equals zero.

123
00:09:11,606 --> 00:09:18,035
Set y to zero: two x equals twelve, so x
equals six. The x intercept is six comma

124
00:09:18,035 --> 00:09:18,432
zero.

125
00:09:19,566 --> 00:09:21,977
The y intercept is where x equals zero.

126
00:09:22,427 --> 00:09:28,059
Three y equals twelve, so y equals four.
The y intercept is zero comma four.

127
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:31,952
Plot both intercepts and draw the line
through them.

128
00:09:32,402 --> 00:09:35,559
That's the fastest way to graph a line in
standard form.

129
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:41,453
To convert from slope-intercept form, move
the x term to the left and clear the

130
00:09:41,453 --> 00:09:42,054
fractions.

131
00:09:42,504 --> 00:09:48,659
y equals one half x plus three. Subtract
one half x: negative one half x plus y

132
00:09:48,659 --> 00:09:49,672
equals three.

133
00:09:50,122 --> 00:09:55,434
Multiply everything by negative two: x
minus two y equals negative six.

134
00:09:56,566 --> 00:10:01,174
Your turn. Find the intercepts of four x
minus five y equals twenty.

135
00:10:01,624 --> 00:10:03,075
Pause the video and try it.

136
00:10:03,525 --> 00:10:10,081
Set y to zero: x equals five. Set x to
zero: negative five y equals twenty, so y

137
00:10:10,081 --> 00:10:11,802
equals negative four.

138
00:10:12,933 --> 00:10:16,837
Let's use standard form and intercepts for
a real budget problem.

139
00:10:18,266 --> 00:10:22,787
Adult tickets cost eight dollars and
student tickets five. A club spends

140
00:10:22,787 --> 00:10:27,809
exactly one hundred twenty dollars. Write
an equation, find both intercepts, and

141
00:10:27,809 --> 00:10:29,253
explain what they mean.

142
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:35,572
Let a be adult tickets and s be student
tickets. Eight a plus five s equals one

143
00:10:35,572 --> 00:10:37,994
hundred twenty. That's standard form.

144
00:10:39,133 --> 00:10:44,061
For the a intercept, set s to zero. Eight
a is one hundred twenty, so a is fifteen.

145
00:10:45,200 --> 00:10:50,621
For the s intercept, set a to zero. Five s
is one hundred twenty, so s is twenty

146
00:10:50,621 --> 00:10:50,960
four.

147
00:10:52,100 --> 00:10:55,662
Plot fifteen, zero and zero, twenty four,
and connect them.

148
00:10:56,800 --> 00:11:01,866
The intercepts are fifteen and twenty
four. Fifteen adult tickets and no student

149
00:11:01,866 --> 00:11:06,805
tickets costs one twenty, or twenty four
student tickets and no adult tickets.

150
00:11:06,933 --> 00:11:12,750
Watch out. To find an intercept, set the
other variable to zero. Standard form

151
00:11:12,750 --> 00:11:17,752
makes that fast. And in this context only
whole number points make sense, because

152
00:11:17,752 --> 00:11:19,666
you can't buy part of a ticket.

153
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:25,637
Your turn. Pens cost two dollars and
notebooks three. You spend thirty. Find

154
00:11:25,637 --> 00:11:28,437
both intercepts. Pause the video and try
it.

155
00:11:32,966 --> 00:11:38,819
Two p plus three n equals thirty. Fifteen
pens and no notebooks, or ten notebooks

156
00:11:38,819 --> 00:11:39,686
and no pens.

157
00:11:40,833 --> 00:11:45,697
In this lesson, we'll use slopes to tell
when lines are parallel or perpendicular.

158
00:11:46,833 --> 00:11:51,377
Parallel lines never meet. They have the
same slope and different y intercepts.

159
00:11:51,827 --> 00:11:57,011
y equals two x plus one, and y equals two
x minus three, are parallel.

160
00:11:58,133 --> 00:12:03,244
Perpendicular lines meet at a right angle.
Their slopes are negative reciprocals:

161
00:12:03,244 --> 00:12:05,642
flip the fraction and change the sign.

162
00:12:06,092 --> 00:12:10,481
If one slope is two thirds, the
perpendicular slope is negative three

163
00:12:10,481 --> 00:12:12,898
halves. Their product is negative one.

164
00:12:14,033 --> 00:12:19,046
Write the line parallel to y equals three
x plus two, through one comma four.

165
00:12:19,496 --> 00:12:25,583
It has the same slope, three. y minus four
equals three times x minus one, so y

166
00:12:25,583 --> 00:12:27,432
equals three x plus one.

167
00:12:28,566 --> 00:12:34,220
Now the line perpendicular to y equals one
half x plus five, through two comma one.

168
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:40,765
The negative reciprocal of one half is
negative two. y minus one equals negative

169
00:12:40,765 --> 00:12:45,336
two times x minus two, so y equals
negative two x plus five.

170
00:12:46,466 --> 00:12:51,721
To classify two lines, compare slopes.
Same slope means parallel. Slopes that

171
00:12:51,721 --> 00:12:56,088
multiply to negative one mean
perpendicular. Otherwise, neither.

172
00:12:56,538 --> 00:13:02,718
For y equals four x minus one and y equals
negative one fourth x plus two, four times

173
00:13:02,718 --> 00:13:07,226
negative one fourth is negative one. So
they're perpendicular.

174
00:13:08,366 --> 00:13:13,593
Your turn. Find the slope of a line
perpendicular to y equals negative five x

175
00:13:13,593 --> 00:13:14,340
plus three.

176
00:13:14,790 --> 00:13:16,240
Pause the video and try it.

177
00:13:16,690 --> 00:13:21,682
Flip negative five and change the sign.
The perpendicular slope is one fifth.

178
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:27,674
Here's a worked example of writing a line
perpendicular to another, through a given

179
00:13:27,674 --> 00:13:28,027
point.

180
00:13:29,467 --> 00:13:34,164
Write the equation of the line
perpendicular to two x plus five y equals

181
00:13:34,164 --> 00:13:36,187
ten, passing through four, one.

182
00:13:37,333 --> 00:13:42,836
First find the slope of the given line.
Solve for y: negative two fifths x plus

183
00:13:42,836 --> 00:13:45,483
two. The slope is negative two fifths.

184
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:51,972
A perpendicular slope is the opposite
reciprocal. Flip two fifths to five halves

185
00:13:51,972 --> 00:13:54,792
and change the sign: positive five halves.

186
00:13:55,933 --> 00:13:58,045
Use point slope form through four, one.

187
00:13:59,167 --> 00:14:05,045
Distribute: five halves x minus ten, then
add one. y equals five halves x minus

188
00:14:05,045 --> 00:14:05,417
nine.

189
00:14:06,567 --> 00:14:10,663
The perpendicular line is y equals five
halves x minus nine.

190
00:14:10,800 --> 00:14:17,282
Watch out. For a perpendicular slope, flip
the fraction and change the sign. Parallel

191
00:14:17,282 --> 00:14:22,119
lines just have the same slope. And
perpendicular slopes always multiply to

192
00:14:22,119 --> 00:14:22,957
negative one.

193
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:29,589
Your turn. Write the line parallel to y
equals negative three x plus one, through

194
00:14:29,589 --> 00:14:32,164
two, five. Pause the video and try it.

195
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:42,890
Same slope, negative three. y minus five
equals negative three times x minus two,

196
00:14:42,890 --> 00:14:46,023
so y equals negative three x plus eleven.

197
00:14:47,166 --> 00:14:52,606
Every linear function is a transformation
of the simplest one, f of x equals x.

198
00:14:53,056 --> 00:14:56,832
In this lesson, we'll see how changing m
and b moves the line.

199
00:14:57,966 --> 00:15:00,227
Changing b shifts the line up or down.

200
00:15:00,677 --> 00:15:07,205
y equals x plus three is the line y equals
x moved up three. y equals x minus two

201
00:15:07,205 --> 00:15:08,656
moves it down two.

202
00:15:09,799 --> 00:15:11,805
Changing m changes the steepness.

203
00:15:12,255 --> 00:15:17,413
When m is bigger than one, the line is
steeper. When m is between zero and one,

204
00:15:17,413 --> 00:15:18,719
the line is flatter.

205
00:15:19,866 --> 00:15:24,559
A negative m flips the line, so it falls
from left to right instead of rising.

206
00:15:25,699 --> 00:15:28,302
Take g of x equals two x minus four.

207
00:15:28,752 --> 00:15:33,125
Start with y equals x, make it twice as
steep, then shift it down four.

208
00:15:34,266 --> 00:15:38,831
In function notation, f of x plus k shifts
the graph up k units.

209
00:15:39,281 --> 00:15:45,239
And a times f of x stretches it when a is
bigger than one. If f of x equals x, then

210
00:15:45,239 --> 00:15:46,961
two f of x equals two x.

211
00:15:48,099 --> 00:15:54,139
Your turn. Describe how y equals negative
one half x plus one compares to y equals

212
00:15:54,139 --> 00:15:54,286
x.

213
00:15:54,736 --> 00:15:56,187
Pause the video and try it.

214
00:15:56,637 --> 00:16:01,191
It's flatter, because one half is less
than one. It falls instead of rising,

215
00:16:01,191 --> 00:16:04,487
because the slope is negative. And it's
shifted up one.

216
00:16:05,633 --> 00:16:09,260
Let's describe how one line is a
transformation of another.

217
00:16:10,733 --> 00:16:16,681
Compare g of x equals negative one half x
plus three to the parent function f of x

218
00:16:16,681 --> 00:16:19,800
equals x, and describe each
transformation.

219
00:16:20,933 --> 00:16:25,594
The slope has size one half, which is less
than one, so the line is less steep.

220
00:16:25,594 --> 00:16:28,485
That's a vertical shrink by a factor of
one half.

221
00:16:29,633 --> 00:16:34,698
The negative sign reflects the line over
the x axis, so it now falls from left to

222
00:16:34,698 --> 00:16:35,073
right.

223
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:41,414
Adding three shifts the line up three
units. The y intercept moves from zero to

224
00:16:41,414 --> 00:16:41,810
three.

225
00:16:42,933 --> 00:16:48,420
So g is f shrunk vertically by one half,
reflected over the x axis, and shifted up

226
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:48,821
three.

227
00:16:49,966 --> 00:16:54,989
Watch out. A slope bigger than one in size
makes the line steeper, and smaller than

228
00:16:54,989 --> 00:17:00,072
one makes it less steep. A negative slope
means a reflection. And adding b moves the

229
00:17:00,072 --> 00:17:02,190
line up, subtracting moves it down.

230
00:17:03,333 --> 00:17:09,251
Your turn. Describe g of x equals three x
minus two compared to f of x equals x.

231
00:17:09,251 --> 00:17:11,248
Pause the video and try it.

232
00:17:15,766 --> 00:17:19,969
It's a vertical stretch by a factor of
three, then a shift down two units.

233
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:26,504
Real data rarely lies exactly on a line.
In this lesson, we'll use scatter plots,

234
00:17:26,504 --> 00:17:28,439
correlation and lines of fit.

235
00:17:29,567 --> 00:17:32,084
A scatter plot shows pairs of data as
points.

236
00:17:32,534 --> 00:17:35,990
Here, each point is a student: hours
studied, and test score.

237
00:17:37,133 --> 00:17:41,436
If the points trend upward, there's a
positive correlation. If they trend

238
00:17:41,436 --> 00:17:43,853
downward, there's a negative correlation.

239
00:17:44,303 --> 00:17:47,119
If there's no pattern at all, there's no
correlation.

240
00:17:48,267 --> 00:17:52,981
A line of fit follows the trend, with
about as many points above it as below it.

241
00:17:53,431 --> 00:17:57,143
Here, a good line of fit is y equals five
x plus sixty.

242
00:17:58,267 --> 00:18:03,958
Use the line to make predictions. For six
hours of study, y equals five times six

243
00:18:03,958 --> 00:18:05,925
plus sixty, which is ninety.

244
00:18:06,375 --> 00:18:08,530
So we predict a score of about ninety.

245
00:18:09,667 --> 00:18:12,525
Be careful: correlation does not mean
causation.

246
00:18:12,975 --> 00:18:17,707
Ice cream sales and sunburns rise
together, but ice cream doesn't cause

247
00:18:17,707 --> 00:18:19,973
sunburns. Hot weather causes both.

248
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:26,436
Your turn. Using y equals five x plus
sixty, predict the score for three hours

249
00:18:26,436 --> 00:18:27,052
of study.

250
00:18:27,502 --> 00:18:28,953
Pause the video and try it.

251
00:18:29,403 --> 00:18:32,261
Five times three, plus sixty, is
seventy-five.

252
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:37,539
Here's a worked example of writing a line
of fit and using it to predict.

253
00:18:38,967 --> 00:18:44,038
Here are study hours and test scores: one
hour, sixty two; two, sixty six; three,

254
00:18:44,038 --> 00:18:49,109
seventy three; four, seventy seven; and
six hours, eighty six. Fit a line through

255
00:18:49,109 --> 00:18:54,305
two, sixty six and six, eighty six, then
predict the score for five hours of study.

256
00:18:55,433 --> 00:18:59,743
First, the points rise from left to right,
so there's a positive correlation.

257
00:19:00,867 --> 00:19:05,884
The slope through our two chosen points is
twenty over four, which is five points per

258
00:19:05,884 --> 00:19:06,179
hour.

259
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:12,655
Point slope form with two, sixty six gives
y equals five x plus fifty six.

260
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:18,280
Predict for five hours: five times five
plus fifty six is eighty one.

261
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:24,453
The line of fit is y equals five x plus
fifty six, and it predicts a score of

262
00:19:24,453 --> 00:19:27,144
about eighty one for five hours of study.

263
00:19:28,267 --> 00:19:33,392
Watch out. Choose two points that follow
the overall trend. Predictions far outside

264
00:19:33,392 --> 00:19:38,024
the data, like twenty hours, aren't
reliable. And correlation doesn't prove

265
00:19:38,024 --> 00:19:40,000
that one thing causes the other.

266
00:19:41,133 --> 00:19:46,524
Your turn. Using y equals five x plus
fifty six, how many hours predict a score

267
00:19:46,524 --> 00:19:49,389
of ninety one? Pause the video and try it.

268
00:19:53,933 --> 00:19:59,847
Ninety one equals five x plus fifty six,
so five x is thirty five and x is seven

269
00:19:59,847 --> 00:20:00,291
hours.

270
00:20:01,433 --> 00:20:06,250
Let's finish Unit Five with a real
decision that uses slope, intercepts and

271
00:20:06,250 --> 00:20:07,470
equations of lines.

272
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:13,809
Company A's table says fifty miles costs
sixty five dollars and one hundred twenty

273
00:20:13,809 --> 00:20:18,599
miles costs eighty six. Company B charges
forty cents a mile plus a forty dollar

274
00:20:18,599 --> 00:20:23,509
base fee. Write both cost lines, find when
they cost the same, and decide which is

275
00:20:23,509 --> 00:20:25,305
cheaper for two hundred miles.

276
00:20:26,433 --> 00:20:30,828
Company A's slope is twenty one over
seventy, or thirty cents per mile.

277
00:20:31,966 --> 00:20:37,726
Using point slope with fifty, sixty five:
A equals zero point three x plus fifty.

278
00:20:37,726 --> 00:20:39,860
The base fee is fifty dollars.

279
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,008
Company B is zero point four x plus forty.

280
00:20:45,133 --> 00:20:47,842
They cost the same when the two
expressions are equal.

281
00:20:48,966 --> 00:20:54,620
Subtract and rearrange: ten equals zero
point one x, so x is one hundred miles.

282
00:20:55,766 --> 00:21:00,438
At two hundred miles, A costs one hundred
ten and B costs one hundred twenty.

283
00:21:01,566 --> 00:21:06,927
The companies cost the same at one hundred
miles, eighty dollars each. Beyond that,

284
00:21:06,927 --> 00:21:10,932
A's smaller slope wins, so A is cheaper
for two hundred miles.

285
00:21:12,066 --> 00:21:17,131
Watch out. The intercept is the fixed fee
and the slope is the per mile rate. Where

286
00:21:17,131 --> 00:21:22,013
the lines cross, the costs are equal. And
the line with the smaller slope always

287
00:21:22,013 --> 00:21:22,989
wins eventually.

288
00:21:24,133 --> 00:21:29,356
Your turn. Gym X charges thirty dollars
plus five per class. Gym Y's table shows

289
00:21:29,356 --> 00:21:34,906
four classes for sixty two dollars and ten
for one hundred ten. When do they cost the

290
00:21:34,906 --> 00:21:37,061
same? Pause the video and try it.

291
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:46,498
Gym Y's slope is forty eight over six,
which is eight, and its intercept is

292
00:21:46,498 --> 00:21:51,983
thirty. Five x plus thirty equals eight x
plus thirty only at zero classes, so Gym X

293
00:21:51,983 --> 00:21:54,400
is cheaper for any number of classes.

294
